Apply ComfyUI scaled-FP8 weight scales when reading safetensors

Bare fp8 tensors are LUT-decoded already, but the per-tensor F32 weight_scale
and scale_weight entries are ignored, so a scaled-FP8 file imports about
1/scale too large and renders a solid colour or NaN.
applyingScaledFP8WeightScales returns the archive itself when a file carries no
scales, and otherwise a wrapper that multiplies each F8_E4M3 tensor by its
matched scale at read time. Wrapping with(_:block:) is what makes it hold for
combined-source gathers whose sources carry different scales, which the
element-level ModelWeightElement.scale affine cannot express. Vetting throws
instead of letting the reader skip silently on orphan scales, scaled E5M2, a
scale entry naming a non-FP8 tensor, and foreign dtypes.
